    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "\"meaningful career\" sounds like a lie we tell people so they don't realize they're just cogs. i don't want a \"solid foundation\" to spend decades doing repetitive tasks. i wanted to be exceptional. if i'm not going to be part of that top 0.1%, then what's even the point? it just feels like i'm wasting time waiting for a life that's never going to happen.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The pursuit of exceptionalism is a powerful drive, but it's also a very exhausting one to carry alone. If the top 0.1% is the only measure of worth, then you've set yourself up for perpetual disappointment. Perhaps the point isn't in achieving the impossible peak, but in finding the deep satisfaction in the *process* of becoming better, even if that \"better\" is just for you.",
      "source": "target",
